WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.736
When workspace automations fail, evidence gets scattered.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:08.170
Train a small fly to find useful files and collect facts for a failure report.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.910
Open Report Scout and create a scout named Failure Scout.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.050
Its learned skill is choosing which file to read next.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.733
In Data, import the supplied space-failures dataset.

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.817
Training, validation, and test workspaces are separate.

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:24.900
Every incident in this collection is synthetic.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.685
In Teach, start a demonstration.

00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:29.871
Select current incident evidence files.

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:35.990
Each click teaches a useful next read; the collection also supplies automatic teaching examples.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.916
Set sixty epochs, learning rate zero point zero five, and seed seventeen.

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:44.160
Train the scout and watch its measured loss curve.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.028
Evaluate held-out cases.

00:00:46.028 --> 00:00:51.942
Compare useful-file coverage with filename matching and random reads, using the same four-read budget.

00:00:51.942 --> 00:00:54.900
These results apply to this synthetic collection.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.912
Run the nightly workspace sync test.

00:00:57.912 --> 00:01:02.333
Its cited records show two authentication-expired errors and one token-refresh failure.

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:05.950
Eight files remain unread, so the report is partial.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.256
The shared credential suggests a connection problem.

00:01:09.256 --> 00:01:15.440
Check token expiry, refresh results, and which jobs share that credential before claiming a root cause.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.387
After evaluation, export the trained JSON.

00:01:18.387 --> 00:01:20.734
It contains the policy and provenance.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:26.210
Running this fly inside xo-space will require the adapter we plan to build next.
